      "message": "This probably should be considered a fatal error. device_is_ready() indicates the driver has been properly registered with the corresponding subsystem.  In this case, \"dev\" is a GPIO driver, so device_is_ready() means all the gpio_*() APIs can be used with this device.\n\nIf the device isn\u0027t ready, then the initialization priorities are incorrect and need to be fixed.\n\nSo returning EC_ERROR_BUSY is possible, or this could halt the system using \"k_oops()\".",
